---
pagination:
  data: redirects
  size: 1
  alias: redirect
permalink: "{{ redirect.from }}"
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
{#- The old address of a page that has moved (listed in
    src/_data/redirects.json). It sends you straight on to the page's new
    address, so old links keep working: GitHub Pages can't redirect by
    itself. The script keeps any #section on the end; the meta tag does the
    same job without it. (The meta tag's address is left plain because the
    build adds /PortfolioWebsite/ to it, as it does to links.) -#}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ site.language }}">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>{{ redirect.title }} &ndash; {{ site.name }}</title>
  <link rel="canonical" href="{{ site.origin }}{{ redirect.to | url }}">
  <script>location.replace({{ redirect.to | url | dump | safe }} + location.hash);</script>
  <meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url={{ redirect.to }}">
</head>
<body>
  <p>This page has moved to <a href="{{ redirect.to }}">{{ redirect.title }}</a>.</p>
</body>
</html>
